---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/schedule';
import venues from '../../data/venues.json';
const tracked = venues.filter((v) => v.enabled);
---

<Layout title="About" current="about">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is a guide to repertory listings and special screenings at the independent theatres of the
      greater San Francisco Bay Area, inspired by <a href="https://screenboston.com">screenboston.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Currently tracking {tracked.map((v, i) => (
        <>
          <a href={v.url}>{v.name}</a>{i < tracked.length - 2 ? ', ' : i === tracked.length - 2 ? ' and ' : ''}
        </>
      ))}.
    </p>
    <p>
      Listings are gathered from the venues' own calendars and checked by hand. Film details and artwork come from
      <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/">TMDB</a>. Always confirm showtimes with the venue.
    </p>
    <p>Built and maintained by <a href="https://www.sunkht.xyz/">Kenneth Sun</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="prose-sub">Feeds and data</h2>
    <p>
      Subscribe to <a href="/feed.xml">/feed.xml</a> for every upcoming screening (one item per film, theatre and day), or to a single
      theatre at <code>/feed/&lt;theatre&gt;.xml</code>, for example {tracked.slice(0, 3).map((v, i) => (
        <>
          <a href={`/feed/${v.id}.xml`}>/feed/{v.id}.xml</a>{i < 2 ? ', ' : ''}
        </>
      ))}.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same data is published as JSON, regenerated with every sync and free to use with attribution:
      <a href="/api/schedule.json">/api/schedule.json</a> (days of cards, as shown here),
      <a href="/api/screenings.json">/api/screenings.json</a> (flat showtimes plus films and venues),
      <a href="/api/films.json">/api/films.json</a>, <a href="/api/venues.json">/api/venues.json</a> and
      <a href="/api/festivals.json">/api/festivals.json</a>. Film metadata and artwork come from TMDB and carry its terms.
    </p>
    <h2 class="prose-sub">Keyboard</h2>
    <p>The schedule can be driven from the keyboard, vim style. Press <kbd>?</kbd> on the schedule page for the full list.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
